# suite TSODESP pick versus despatch
ok 1 - a pick list needs an order number
ok 2 - AC-044 picking never moves stock
ok 3 - AC-044 picking never creates a cost of sale
ok 4 - AC-044 picking never despatches a quantity
ok 5 - an unknown pick function reports PCK0008
ok 6 - a confirmation needs a correlation id
ok 7 - a confirmation needs at least one line
ok 8 - an unknown despatch function reports DSP0008
ok 9 - a reversal needs authority and a reason
ok 10 - a refused despatch posts no cost of sale
ok 11 - a released order generates a pick list
ok 12 - the pick list carries the one open schedule
ok 13 - the required quantity is the schedule quantity
ok 14 - AC-044 generating a pick list moves no stock
ok 15 - a short pick without a reason is refused
ok 16 - a reasoned short pick is accepted with a warning
ok 17 - AC-044 the short quantity is recorded
ok 18 - AC-044 the outstanding demand survives
ok 19 - AC-044 picking creates no stock movement
ok 20 - AC-044 the order line is still undespatched
ok 21 - AC-044 the schedule is still undespatched
ok 22 - printing increments the print count
ok 23 - reprinting increments it again and nothing else
ok 24 - reprinting moves no stock
ok 25 - reprinting creates no stock movement
ok 26 - SO-013 the line is judged, not the missing bin
ok 27 - SO-013 the despatch names the bin it would take from
ok 28 - SO-013 the defaulted bin holds owned accepted stock
ok 29 - AC-044 a repeat confirmation is not a second effect
ok 30 - AC-044 the repeat is reported as a duplicate
ok 31 - AC-044 the original despatch is returned
ok 32 - AC-044 the original cost of sale is unchanged
ok 33 - AC-044 no second stock movement was created
ok 34 - AC-044 no second despatch was created
